      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9344637393951416,
      "reading_order": 9,
      "text": "7. The atomic size of an element is inversely pro-\nportional to its effective nuclear charge. This\nis because increase in effective nuclear charge\nincreases the nuclear force of attraction on the\noutermost shell and hence, the lesser atomic size.\nHence, the correct option is (d)."
